Reason:
The condition checks for active elements were incorrectly applied in multiple scenarios, which caused the code to enter an endless loop when trying to re-insert an inactive element into the red-black tree without selecting a next branch for inspection.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (nft_rbtree_interval_end(rbe) &&
    !nft_rbtree_interval_end(new)) {
    p = &parent->rb_left;
} else if (!nft_rbtree_interval_end(rbe) &&
           nft_rbtree_interval_end(new)) {
    p = &parent->rb_right;
} else if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    *ext = &rbe->ext;
    return -EEXIST;
} else {
    p = &parent->rb_left;
}
```
Reason:
The patch restricts the checks for active elements to only the case where an element already exists (EEXIST), thus preventing the endless loop by ensuring that the next branch is always selected appropriately based on the conditions of the elements being compared.

